\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  ends  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Antonio de la Jara   \par \uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2008\par 23:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with fresh quotes, peso data)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Sept 29 (Reuters) - Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday called an early halt to an $8 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan that has seen the peso depreciate 22 percent since April, citing international financial turmoil.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the program, under which it bought $50 million worth of greenbacks daily, was 70 percent complete. The plan was originally introduced in April to reverse a sharp appreciation of the peso <CLP=CL> <CHILJ> earlier in the year.\par \par \uc2 "In recent days, there has been a significant deterioration in international financial markets. Due to this, the board has decided today to end its program to accumulate reserves," the bank said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had increased international reserves to the tune of $5.75 billion under the program.\par \par \uc2 "The Chilean economy remains prepared to adequately face turbulence in international markets," it added.\par \par \uc2 The bank also said it would resume a program of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps from Tuesday, which were replaced by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program.\par \par \uc2 The peso skidded on Monday to a three-year low as prices for copper -- Chile's main export -- fell below $3 a pound and investors worried that a global financial crisis could deepen.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed 2.23 percent lower at 551.50/552.00 pesos per dollar, compared with its close at 539.20/539.70 on Friday. It was the peso's weakest close since August 2005.\par \par \uc2 The peso fell to 558.7 pesos per dollar in after-hours trade following rejection of a U.S. financial sector rescue plan.\par \par \uc2 The peso has now depreciated over 10 percent in the year-to-date.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would continue to use all instruments at its disposal to ensure financial stability and the normal flow of payments.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised its policy interest rates to their highest levels in around a decade in recent months in a bid to curb inflation which is running at its quickest since 1994.\par \par \uc2 Annual inflation is currently over 9.0 percent, or three times the bank's target. (Writing by Simon Gardner; editing by Gary Crosse)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 -END (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080929e49t0020h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
