\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Chile peso tumbles in early trade in market downturn\b0\par\par\uc2 186 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2008\par 14:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds further peso falls)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Sept 16 (Reuters) - Chile's peso tumbled 2.6 percent against the dollar in early trade on Tuesday and hit a 19-month low as turmoil swept global markets.\par \par \uc2 The peso <CHILJ> <CLP=CL> fell to 545.20/545.70 per dollar, from its closer on Monday at 532.00/538.80 per dollar as regional markets fell for a second day and the price of copper, Chile's chief export, fell.\par \par \uc2 "Again we have European and Asian markets in the negative and U.S. stock futures are anticipating a depressing start to the day because of the financial crisis in the United States," one trader said.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's fall represented the sharpest decline in the peso since April 11, the day after \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced an $8 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it hit levels near 430 pesos per dollar. (Reporting by Maria Jose Latorre and Rodrigo Martinez; Editing by Tom Hals)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-PESO/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080916e49g001gr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
