\par\par \b \uc2 Chile peso firms against dollar, stocks edge higher\b0\par\par\uc2 By Froilan Romero and Manuel Farias   \par \uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 2008\par 21:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Aug 27 (Reuters) - Chile's peso rose on Wednesday amid strong dollar sales on the domestic market, while stocks ended slightly firmer but off the day's highs as gains on Wall Street buoyed regional bourses.\par \par \uc2 The peso <CHILJ> <CLP=CL>, which has depreciated strongly since an $8 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this year, gained 0.52 percent against the dollar to 519.50/520.00 pesos per dollar, versus Tuesday's close at 522.20/522.50 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "From the start of the day there were a lot of dollars on offer by pension funds, and the dollar weakened at the same time, leading to a rise in the peso," one trader said.\par \par \uc2 The peso has depreciated 4.18 percent so far this year against the dollar, after appreciating 6.44 percent in 2007. However, it has depreciated around 17 percent since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April to sap strength from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's all-market IGPA stock index <.IGPA> ended 0.14 percent firmer at 13,785.93 points, while the blue-chip IPSA <.IPSA> firmed 0.12 percent at 2,897.83 points.\par \par \uc2 Shares of Chile steel and iron ore producer Cap rose for a second day, up 2.35 percent to 18,600 pesos per share. The company is in a $550 million expansion of its sheet steel \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stock of leading fertilizer exporter Soquimich , also rose for another day, up 2.61 percent at 20,485 pesos per share.\par \par \uc2 However retailers were weaker, with D&S , owner of Chile's biggest supermarket chain, falling 0.32 percent and diversified retailer \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  falling 2.37 percent to 1,470 pesos.\par \par \uc2 Shares in Chile-based regional energy group \uc2 Enersis\uc2  fell 0.46 percent to 179 pesos.\par \par \uc2 Chile's largest bank, Santander Santiago , saw a 1.23 percent rise in its stock price after announcing Jan-July profit of 186.63 billion pesos ($371 million). (Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHILE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080827e48r0026m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
