\par\par \b \uc2 Analysts see Chile peso settling by year end\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lisa Yulkowski   \par \uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2008\par 16:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, July 10 (Reuters) - Most analysts see the Chilean peso converging at about 500 per dollar at year end, as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program expires and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  re-establishes its inflation-fighting credentials by raising rates.\par \par \uc2 The greenback started the year at near 500 pesos, slumped to 430 pesos in March, but after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kicked off an $8 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April to curb the strength of the peso the dollar scaled to a high of 529 pesos in June.\par \par \uc2 Six \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts and economists estimated the value of the dollar at year-end would be between 485 pesos and 530 pesos, but said the level would be influenced by several factors, including the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , oil and food prices, interest rates, inflation and the policies of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bertrand Delgado, senior economist and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with IDEAglobal in New York, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has complicated projections.\par \par \uc2 He sees the peso at about 506 per dollar at the end of the year, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fights inflation, but said it could strengthen to 485 depending on the bank's decisions.\par \par \uc2 "A few months ago the bank practically subordinated its monetary policy to the exchange rate policy. That's why the peso weakened so much," Delgado said. "That gives me a certain degree of assurance that they're going to raise rates and focus on inflation now."\par \par \uc2 Pedro Tuesta a senior Latam analyst with 4CAST in Washington sees the peso at 530 per dollar, given a reduction in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and moderately aggressive interest rate increases to 7.5 percent by year end.\par \par \uc2 "(The problem is) the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is temporary, it will change over time, and it's taking place in a highly inflationary context, so it's working against the bank's monetary policy."\par \par \uc2 Analysts say that while exporters benefit from a cheaper domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rest of the economy is getting walloped with even higher inflation.\par \par \uc2 INFLATION PRESSURES AND \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's consumer price index rose 1.5 percent in June, bringing 12-month inflation to 9.5 percent, its highest level since 1994.\par \par \uc2 The figure reinforced expectations the bank would hike its key rate by 50 basis points for a second month in a row to 7.25 percent on Thursday to control runaway inflation, which has helped the peso to appreciate to 504 per dollar despite the continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "They're depreciating the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a time when inflationary pressures keep rising. That's very dangerous," said Delgado.\par \par \uc2 Barclays Capital Research does not see the bank suspending the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite the problems it may be creating with inflation and sees the peso at 485 per dollar at year end.\par \par \uc2 "We do not expect an interruption of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, as the rules-based Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be very reluctant to modify it," \uc2 Barclays\uc2  said in a report. "We think the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program is largely priced in at this point."\par \par \uc2 Tomas Flores, a local economist with the Instituto de Libertad y Desarrollo also thinks the bank is unlikely to change course on its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Our view is that they never should have started, but now that they have, its not easy to get out of it. They're stuck." (Additional Reporting by Maria Jose Latorre; Editing by Tom Hals)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-PESO/|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|RNP|DNP|PCM   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080710e47a001b6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
