\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS- \highlight22\uc2 Chile central bank \highlight\uc2  seen clipping  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lisa Yulkowski   \par \uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2008\par 18:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, June 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to scrap its $8 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  only two months after its launch, as rising oil prices and a weaker peso are pushing up inflation, making it counterproductive.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , implemented in April after the peso appreciated some 16 percent year-to-date against the beleaguered U.S. dollar, achieved its goal of curbing the peso's strength, but a rebound in the dollar has now undermined the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "At the time it was a good decision, but the situation changed," said Rodrigo Aravena, an economist with the Banchile brokerage . "The plan was probably to take the level to about 460 to 470 pesos, but they hadn't considered that oil prices would rise so much."\par \par \uc2 After ending last year at 498 pesos, the dollar fell to 430 pesos in March and since the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recovered, ending at 497 pesos on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 In early April, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was announced, prices for oil were at just above $100 per barrel and the dollar was in a global slump.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  included buying $50 million dollars daily on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange until the end of the year, a commitment the bank has continued to honor despite high inflation.\par \par \uc2 CONTROLLING INFLATION\par \par \uc2 Chile imports nearly all of the fuel it consumes and the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the peso's strength, on top of the effect of soaring oil prices, and a stronger dollar, hit Chile with even higher than expected inflation in May of 1.2 percent.\par \par \uc2 The Bank's response this week was to raise the benchmark interest rate an aggressive 50 basis points to 6.75 percent, its first increase since January.\par \par \uc2 The decision underscored the change in focus from the exchange rate to inflation, and called into question the effects of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The problem is if the peso depreciates too fast it tends to pressure inflation... and this is getting too fast." said Pedro Tuesta, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with 4CAST in Washington.\par \par \uc2 "They probably won't stop (the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) right away, because they are committed month to month," he said. "But it doesn't make sense any more."\par \par \uc2 The peso has depreciated nearly 13 percent since just before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was announced in April.\par \par \uc2 Aravena also said the bank would avoid any sudden changes after this week's rate surprise, but said he did not see the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continuing as it has.\par \par \uc2 "Having two surprises together could be costly. It would be more prudent to wait a bit and then reduce the amount of dollars they are buying or eliminate it," he said.\par \par \uc2 "We might have a few more months of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but I really doubt it will last the year."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not giving any indication it is thinking of pruning back the measure.\par \par \uc2 The bank, in its third monthly phase of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , should announce its plans for the next phase before July 8. (Additional reporting by Froilan Romero)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -PESO/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080613e46d001ve\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
