\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk Pres: Satisfied With  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2008\par 19:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with more comments from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president and executive)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Jose De Gregorio said Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "satisfied" with its announced \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Last month, in a bid to weaken the peso - which was trading at 10-year highs - the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it would increase its international reserves by $8 billion by the end of the year through daily purchases of $50 million.\par \par \uc2 Since the bank began its daily purchases on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in mid-April, the peso has weakened nearly 8%.\par \par \uc2 "We are very satisfied with the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program and it's coherent with our inflationary objective," De Gregorio told reporters.\par \par \uc2 He added that the bank currently has no plans to increase its purchases and if it did, it would announce it in due course, just like it announced this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before it began its daily purchases.\par \par \uc2 To prevent an inflationary expansion in money supply, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is sterilizing the dollar purchases by issuing short-term debt during the first month of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it would increase by $3.0 billion its local debt offerings during the next three months to sterilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The announcement of the additional $3 billion sent long-term \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond yields shooting up 40 basis points and analysts fear that these yield increases will spill over into higher mortgage rates.\par \par \uc2 The yields on inflation-indexed 10-year bonds have risen nearly 40 basis points in the past few sessions, reaching 3.4%-3.42% earlier this week. By Friday, they saw a correction to 3.19%-3.21%.\par \par \uc2 De Gregorio said he couldn't rule out that the fixed-income market had overreacted to the bond issue announcement. He said he expects \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond yields to continue correcting downwards in coming sessions.\par \par \uc2 "These (yield hikes) should normalize in the short-term and these (corrections) will be the ones that will have repercutions on long-term home and corporate financing; mortage rates won't be reacting to what's happening in yield rates within the short span of a week," De Gregorio said.\par \par \uc2 Early this week, Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its 2008 gross domestic product estimate to 4%-5% with a downside risk, from a previous 4.5%-5.5% estimate. Analysts, meanwhile, expect 4% GDP growth this year.\par \par \uc2 In the first quarter of 2008, the Imacec economic growth index, a GDP proxy, posted a 3.3% on-year gain. The bank will release the first-quarter GDP later this month.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects growth to pick up in the second half of the year.\par \par \uc2 "Just on the effects of the basis of comparison, second-half growth should be higher than in the first half of the year," the bank's head of research, Pablo Garcia, told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Chile's GDP grew 5.1% in 2007, up from 4.3% in 2006. GDP in the first six months of 2007 grew 6.2% on the year, but decelerated to a 4% on-year gain in the second half.\par \par \uc2 -By Patricia San Juan and Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-460-8544; chile@dowjones.com [ 16-05-08 1724GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080516e45g000x9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
