\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  cenbank chief happy with  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2008\par 17:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quote, details from fourth paragraph)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, May 16 (Reuters) - Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is happy with the progress of its $8 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program to curb the strong peso, bank president Jose De Gregorio said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The program "is proceeding as we expected it to," De Gregorio told reporters after a business forum in the capital Santiago. "The system is working. We are happy with this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program."\par \par \uc2 The bank announced the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April after the peso firmed nearly 16 percent against the dollar in 2008, and has been buying $50 million worth of dollars a day in auctions.\par \par \uc2 Since then, the peso <CLP=CL> <CHILJ> has pared its appreciation versus the greenback to about 7 percent year-to-date.\par \par \uc2 "This program of accumulating (dollar) reserves will allow us to better confront any additional, abrupt and severe deterioration in the foreign environment," De Gregorio said.\par \par \uc2 Economists say this type of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tends to worsen domestic inflationary pressures, but De Gregorio said the measure was "coherent with our inflation objectives."\par \par \uc2 Chile's 12-month inflation slowed to 8.3 percent in April, but is still well above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's medium-term target rate of 3 percent. (Reporting by Antonio de la Jara, Writing by Simon Gardner; Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-ECONOMY/CENBANK (UPDATE 1)|LAN