\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends 1% Stronger; Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Shrugged Off\b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolina Pica   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2008\par 20:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso ended 1.0% stronger against the U.S. dollar Wednesday, shrugging off the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily $50 million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended trading at CLP444.80 to the dollar, compared with CLP449.20 at Tuesday's close, after trading in a range of CLP443.30-CLP448.45.\par \par \uc2 According to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which compiles its own estimate of the day's range, the dollar fetched CLP445.69 at 1600 GMT, about an hour before the session ended.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $50 million through a daily tender at 1430 GMT. The bank, on its Web site, said it received offers totaling $194 million. It purchased the $50 million at prices ranging from CLP446.30 to CLP446.35. The average peso price it paid for the $50 million was CLP446.32, the bank said.\par \par \uc2 The peso strengthened on the greenback's weakness abroad, in relation to other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and on copper prices flirting with the $4-a-pound mark.\par \par \uc2 Chile is the world's largest copper producer. Exports of the red metal represent about 65% of the country's exports and are a significant revenue generator. Currently, a contract workers strike at state copper giant \uc2 Corporacion Nacional del Cobre de Chile\uc2 , among other factors, is underpinning copper prices.\par \par \uc2 The peso could strengthen to CLP440 in coming sessions if the dollar fails to recover abroad and if copper prices continue to climb, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 On the local bond market, yields on Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds five-year BCUs closed higher on private pension fund managers' selective selling, in an otherwise thin session, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The yield on inflation-indexed five-year BCUs ended at 2.32%, up from 2.3% Tuesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.7%, unchanged.\par \par \uc2 Over the next few days, five-year BCU yields could move between 2.25% and 2.35%, while 10-year BCU yields could fluctuate between 2.68% and 2.73%, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-460-8544; carolina.pica@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Patricia San Juan contributed to this report.) [ 23-04-08 1819GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080423e44n0012v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
