\par\par \b \uc2 Chile cenbank buys $50 mln at average 456.92 pesos each\b0\par\par\uc2 143 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2008\par 16:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, April 18 (Reuters) - Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $50 million worth of dollars at an average price of 456.92 pesos each on Friday, the latest stage of its $8 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program aimed at reverting the peso's sharp appreciation earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 The bank received offers totalling $105 million at a competitive auction, it said on its official Web site {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bcentral.cl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bcentral.cl}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank aims to boost foreign reserves and curb peso <CLP=CL> <CHILJ> strength by buying $8 billion on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by Dec. 12.\par \par \uc2 The bank announced its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program on April 10 after the peso in 2008 had strengthend as much as 15 percent against the dollar. (Writing by Simon Gardner)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080421e44i001dr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
