\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Chile central banker: rate rise, fall equally likely\b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 2008\par 18:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with fresh quotes, details)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, April 14 (Reuters) - Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio said on Monday he saw equal chances of an increase or a cut in the bank's official interest rates and said a major new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program was "exceptional."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised its benchmark rate five times since July in a bid to control accelerating inflation, while the U.S. Federal Reserve has slashed its key rate to 2.25 percent to stave off recession.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its benchmark rate steady at 6.25 percent this month for a third month in a row.\par \par \uc2 "According to the latest data available, our view is that it is equally likely the rate will rise or fall in the future," he said in a speech to the Chilean-American Chamber of Commerce in Washington.\par \par \uc2 "The recent decisions of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  do not rule out future increases in policy rates, but it is equally likely there could be reductions."\par \par \uc2 Comparatively higher interest rates in Chile than in the United States make the peso an attractive investment, and sky-high copper prices are contributing to strong trade surpluses.\par \par \uc2 That has sparked a sharp appreciation of the peso, creating another headache.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week announced an $8 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program aimed at weakening the peso, and on Monday bought the first daily installment of $50 million worth of greenbacks.\par \par \uc2 It was the first time the bank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since 2002.\par \par \uc2 The peso hit a decade high of 431.20/431.50 on March 18 to trade around 15 percent higher for the year-to-date, the strongest level since late 1997.\par \par \uc2 The peso stayed close to that level, sparking a cry from Chilean exporters who fear the loss of their competitive edge worldwide. On Friday, however, the peso fell 2.8 percent on news of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan.\par \par \uc2 "It is an exceptional measure," De Gregorio said. "There is an explicit commitment not to try to fix the value, or range, of the exchange rate, thus reducing the space for speculation."\par \par \uc2 Inflation is also an obstacle.\par \par \uc2 Chile's consumer price index rose a milder-than-expected 0.8 percent in March, but the reading still pushed annual inflation to a 14-year high of 8.5 percent from 8.1 percent the prior month.\par \par \uc2 "What we are signaling with this (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) measure is that our inflation targets and current monetary policy framework can accommodate a depreciation of the peso, something we could not have been sure of a couple of months back," De Gregorio said. (Reporting by Rodrigo Martinez, Writing by Simon Gardner; Editing by Tom Hals)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-ECONOMY/CENTRALBANK (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080417e44e001vf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
