\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-EXCLUSIVE- \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  cbank starts  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , buys $50 mln\b0\par\par\uc2 By Rodrigo Martinez   \par \uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 2008\par 17:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds details throughout)\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, April 14 (Reuters) - Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday launched an $8 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at curbing the peso's sharp appreciation, buying the first daily installment of $50 million worth of greenbacks.\par \par \uc2  A bank official told Reuters that the bank bought the dollars at an average price of 449.63 pesos each and that it received offers totaling $103 million.\par \par \uc2  It was the first time the bank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since 2002.\par \par \uc2  The peso was little moved in early Monday trade following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The peso closed 2.8 percent lower on Friday, the day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement, at 446.30/446.80 per dollar. <CLP=CL> <CHILJ>\par \par \uc2  The bank aims to boost foreign reserves and combat the sharp rise in the peso by buying $8 billion worth of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  via competitive auctions from April 14 to Dec. 12.\par \par \uc2  The bank announced the move last week after the peso had appreciated 15 percent in the year to date against the dollar, trading at its highest level in more than a decade.\par \par \uc2  The peso hit a decade high of 431.20/431.50 on March 18, the strongest level since late 1997, and has stayed close to that level since, sparking a cry from Chilean exporters fearing the loss of their competitive edge worldwide.\par \par \uc2  Comparatively higher interest rates in Chile than in the United States make the peso a more attractive investment, and sky-high copper prices are maintaining strong trade surpluses.\par \par \uc2  The government has welcomed the move. However, some analysts are not convinced that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy will have a profound effect.  (Writing by Simon Gardner; Editing by Jonathan Oatis)   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1, EXCLUSIVE)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080417e44e001ol\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
