\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  govt welcomes  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  peso  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 150 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2008\par 16:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, April 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government on Friday welcomed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb the peso's sharp appreciation against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The government values the decision ... taken by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to accumulate international reserves," Finance Minister Andres Velasco told a news conference.\par \par \uc2 "I am convinced the decision adopted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will contribute to the competitiveness of the economy and correct this disalignement (in the exchange rate)," he added.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said late on Thursday it would buy $8 billion worth of dollars this year to build up foreign reserves and combat the sharp rise of the peso against the dollar. (Reporting by Rodrigo Martinez, Writing by Simon Gardner; Editing by Theodore d'Afflisio)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-ECONOMY/VELASCO (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080411e44b001c5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
