\par\par \b \uc2 TEXT- \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  cenbank to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  market\b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2008\par 03:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, April 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to boost liquidity in the economy and in response to the local peso's <CLP=CL> <CHILJ> sharp appreciation against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement the "exceptional measure" aims to boost foreign reserves by $8 billion by buying dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, in the period from April 14 to Dec. 12.\par \par \uc2 Following is the text of the statement.\par \par \uc2 The complex scenario that financial markets in developed economies are going through, triggered by the crisis in the United States real estate market, has increased the risk of severe disruptions that could negatively impact the external financial conditions faced by the Chilean economy.\par \par \uc2 The macroeconomic framework based on a floating exchange rate, inflation targeting, a fiscal rule and prudential financial supervision puts the Chilean economy in a favorable position to weather these turbulences. Nevertheless, the depth and consequences of an international financial crisis remain highly uncertain.\par \par \uc2 With these concerns in mind, the Board of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  today decided to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market so as to strengthen the external liquidity position of the Chilean economy.\par \par \uc2 This increase in the stock of international reserves will leave the Chilean economy better prepared to face the eventuality of an additional, severe and abrupt deterioration of the external environment.\par \par \uc2 In the inflation targeting and exchange rate flexibility framework put in in September 2nd 1999, this exceptional measure is justified by the unusual degree of uncertainty regarding events in international financial markets.\par \par \uc2 It is also coherent with the evaluation that the real exchange rate is currently below the level that would prevail once real and financial conditions in the world economy return to normal.\par \par \uc2 The Board of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2  has adopted the following measure:\par \par \uc2 To increase the stock of international reserves by US$ 8000 million, by purchasing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the period extending from April 14th to December 12th 2008.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2  will, in due course, announce the specific purchase programs, which could be modified according to market conditions. The first program, which will run from April 14th to May 9th will consist of daily purchases of around US$ 50 million via competitive auctions.\par \par \uc2 The monetary effects of this measure will be offset so that liquidity provision is consistent with the monetary policy rate. During the period comprising the first program mentioned above this will be done with short term \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This exceptional measure is coherent with the overall conduct of monetary policy, which aims to keep inflation at 3% most of the time, with a tolerance range of +/- 1%.\par \par \uc2 The current monetary policy rate allows the convergence of the current high current inflation rates to 3% over the policy horizon. Monetary policy actions, in one direction or the other, cannot be ruled out in response to future changes in inflation prospects.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2  will continue to use all of the tools at its disposal in pursuit of the objectives assigned to it by law. (Editing by Carol Bishopric)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-ECONOMY/CENBANK-TEXT|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080411e44b0001w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
