\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends 2.8% Weaker After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Announcement\b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolina Pica   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2008\par 19:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso ended 2.8% weaker against the dollar Friday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced an $8 billion market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan late Thursday, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended trading at CLP446.40 to the dollar, compared with CLP433.70 at Thursday's close, after trading in a range of CLP446.40-CLP451.00.\par \par \uc2 According to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which compiles its own estimate of the day's range, the dollar fetched CLP449.77 at 1600 GMT, about an hour before the session ended.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it would increase its stock of international reserves by $8 billion by purchasing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , namely dollars, from April 14 through Dec. 12 this year.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2  will, in due course, announce the specific purchase programs, which could be modified according to market conditions. The first program, which will run from April 14 to May, will consist of daily purchases of around $50 million via competitive auctions," the bank said in a statement Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Next week, the peso will likely trade in a CLP440-CLP460 range as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  begins its daily purchases, according to IDEAglobal Inc. economist Bertrand Delgado.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement, on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held the key interest rate steady, for the third consecutive month, at 6.25%. It also changed its policy bias to neutral from a previous tightening bias.\par \par \uc2 On the local bond market, yields on Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds closed lower in reaction to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to leave the key rate pat.\par \par \uc2 The yield on inflation-indexed five-year BCUs ended at 2.13%, down from 2.16% Thursday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.61%, down from 2.63% Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Over the next few days, five-year BCU yields could move between 2.1% and 2.2%, while 10-year BCU yields could fluctuate between 2.6% and 2.68%, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-460-8544; carolina.pica@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Patricia San Juan contributed to this report) [ 11-04-08 1758GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080411e44b000ug\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
