\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Govt Commends Ctrl Bank Peso Market  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Plan\b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2008\par 19:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chilean Finance Minister Andres Velasco Friday applauded the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, adding the move will help correct the peso's real exchange rate with respect to its fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 "I'm convinced that the measure the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced will contribute to our economy's competitiveness and correct this misalignment (of the exchange rate in real terms)," Velasco told reporters.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced plans for an $8 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stop the peso's strengthening against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Before the measure was announced, the peso had gained more than 12% against the dollar, reaching 10-year highs in recent weeks. It strengthened on record prices of copper, the country's main export, and the four-percentage-point differential between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key TPM interest rate and the U.S. federal funds rate.\par \par \uc2 The minister reiterated he agreed with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's outlook that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had overreacted to these aforementioned factors and that the exchange rate, in real terms, in recent weeks didn't correspond with its fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 With regard to the possible impact of the peso's tumble on inflation, Velasco said "the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been very clear about that and I don't have anything to add to that in the sense that this decision is in line with its mandate for inflationary stability."\par \par \uc2 The Finance Minister declined to respond to queries on whether the government will implement additional measures to further weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He reiterated the government's policy is to save the fiscal surplus in overseas accounts to avoid pressuring the peso to strengthen.\par \par \uc2 When asked about the initial \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market reaction to the move, in which the peso lost 3.5% in early trading versus its Thursday closing price, Velasco said he commended the reaction, but wouldn't comment any further on peso trading levels.\par \par \uc2 About an hour before peso trading is slated to close, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trading at CLP447.90 to the dollar, versus CLP433.70 at Thursday's close.\par \par \uc2 -By Patricia San Juan, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-460-8546; patty.sanjuan@dowjones.com [ 11-04-08 1705GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080411e44b000u5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
