\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  cenbank to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  market\b0\par\par\uc2 628 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2008\par 01:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Updates with economist quote, details)\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, April 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to boost liquidity in the economy and in response to the local peso's <CLP=CL> <CHILJ> sharp appreciation against the dollar.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement the "exceptional measure" aims to boost foreign reserves by $8 billion by buying dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, in the period from April 14 to Dec. 12.\par \par \uc2  For the first four weeks, it would buy $50 million a day through competitive auctions.\par \par \uc2  The peso has appreciated 15 percent this year against the dollar to trade at its highest level in more than a decade, as comparatively higher interest rates make the peso a more attractive investment and sky-high copper prices maintain strong trade surpluses.\par \par \uc2  "The complex scenario that financial markets in developed economies are going through, triggered by the crisis in the United States' real estate market, has increased the risk of severe disruptions that could negatively impact the external financial conditions faced by the Chilean economy," the bank said in an e-mailed statement.\par \par \uc2  "The depth and consequences of an international financial crisis remain highly uncertain," it added. "With these concerns in mind, the Board of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  today decided to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market so as to strengthen the external liquidity position of the Chilean economy."\par \par \uc2  Chile's consumer price index rose a milder-than-expected 0.8 percent in March, but the reading still pushed annual inflation to a 14-year high of 8.5 percent from 8.1 percent the prior month. Economic growth also picked up in February to 5.6 percent.\par \par \uc2  Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised its benchmark rate five times since July in a bid to control surging inflation, while the U.S. Federal Reserve has slashed its key rate to 2.25 percent to stave off recession.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held the target overnight lending rate at 6.25 percent for a third month in a row at its monthly monetary policy meeting on Thursday, in a decision widely expected by the local market.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement was not.\par \par \uc2  "It is a dangerous bet, because it could lose a lot of money," said Tomas Flores, an economist with the Instituto Libertad y Desarrollo think-tank, forecasting the exchange rate could weaken more than 10 percent against the dollar on Friday.\par \par \uc2  "It is similar to what happened almost a decade ago, when there was a band with a floor and a ceiling for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The difference is that now there is no explicit band," he added.\par \par \uc2  The bank said an increase in the stock of Chile's international reserves would leave its economy better prepared to face the eventuality of "an additional, severe and abrupt deterioration of the external environment," the bank added.\par \par \uc2  "This exceptional measure is justified by the unusual degree of uncertainty regarding events in international financial markets. It is also coherent with the evaluation that the real exchange rate is currently below the level that would prevail once real and financial conditions in the world economy return to normal."\par \par \uc2  The bank said its plan was also in keeping with its conduct of monetary policy, which aims to keep inflation at 3 percent, within a range of one percentage point either way.\par \par \uc2  "Monetary policy actions, in one direction or the other, cannot be ruled out in response to future changes in inflation prospects," the bank said.  (Reporting by Manuel Farias and Antonio de la Jara; Writing by Simon Gardner; Editing by Gary Hill)   \par \par \uc2 CHILE-ECONOMY/CENBANK (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080410e44a002b3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
