\par\par \b \uc2 Chile  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  chief won't be rushed on peso   \b0\par\par\uc2 254 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2008\par 21:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, April 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not ruled out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cool the sharply appreciating peso, the bank's president reiterated on Wednesday, but it will not be pushed into making hasty decisions on the issue.   \par \par \uc2 Addressing a special Senate session on the exchange rate, bank President Jose De Gregorio said he stood by the peso's free-floating regime against the dollar at a time when exporters are calling for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 It was De Gregorio's third signal to the market in a fortnight.   \par \par \uc2 "We have not ruled out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," De Gregorio said. "These things are not announced.   \par \par \uc2 "We are constantly evaluating both the costs and benefits and effectiveness of such a measure, as we don't want to make rushed decisions which weaken our macroeconomic policy."   \par \par \uc2 The peso <CLP=> <CHILJ> has appreciated around 14 percent against the dollar so far this year, trading around its highest levels in over a decade on high international copper prices and a gaping interest rate differential with the United States.   \par \par \uc2 The peso's ascent is hitting farmers, who export most of their fruits and vegetables to buyers who pay in dollars. With the weaker dollar, the revenues do not go as far as they once did in paying peso-denominated costs like labor. (Reporting by Rodrigo Martinez, writing by Simon Gardner; Editing by Dan Grebler)   \par \par \uc2 