\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Peso  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  an option, warns  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  cenbank   \b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 15:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with fresh details, peso gain)   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, March 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not ruled out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cool the sharply appreciating peso, President Jose De Gregorio said on Wednesday, warning speculators there would be no bailout if they get burnt.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not going to come to the rescue of those who are speculating about where they think the exchange rate is going," De Gregorio told a business seminar in Santiago.   \par \par \uc2 The peso <CLP=> <CHILJ> has appreciated nearly 12 percent against the dollar so far this year, trading around its highest levels in over a decade on the back of high international copper prices and a gaping interest rate differential with the United States.   \par \par \uc2 It was De Gregorio's second signal to the market in just over a week. Last week he cautioned the bank would avoid any hasty action to curb the peso's gains but warned the option of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained on the table.   \par \par \uc2 The peso's ascent is hitting farmers who export most of their fruits and vegetables to buyers who pay in dollars.   \par \par \uc2 With the weaker dollar, the revenues don't go as far as they once did in paying peso-denominated costs like labor.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <CHILJ><CLP=CL> extended its rally on Wednesday, gaining 1.17 percent to 445.40/445.90 by 1139 local (1439 gmt).   \par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised its benchmark rate to 6.25 percent to control inflation, while the Fed has lowered rates to try to jump-start the weak U.S. economy.   \par \par \uc2 By contrast, the U.S. Federal Reserve slashed U.S. interest rates last week by three-quarters of a percentage point, taking the benchmark overnight rate down to 2.25 percent, the lowest since February 2005.   \par \par \uc2 De Gregorio said there was no evidence to suggest that carry trades were behind the peso's appreciation.   \par \par \uc2 Carry trades involve borrowing in low interest rate \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the Japanese yen to investor in higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets. (Reporting by Rodrigo Martinez, writing by Simon Gardner, editing by Walker Simon)   \par \par \uc2 CHILE-CENBANK/PESO (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080326e43q0010i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
