\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Chile  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  sees lower growth,higher prices   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Antonio de la Jara and Rodrigo Martinez   \par \uc2 584 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2008\par 14:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts lead, adds comment on non-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , paragraph 12)   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO/VALPARAISO, Jan 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday cut its 2008 economic growth estimates to between 4.5 and 5.5 percent, and signaled higher interest rates were on the horizon as the inflation outlook climbed.   \par \par \uc2 In a speech to Chile's Congress in the port city of Valparaiso, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Jose de Gregorio said the bank was "deeply upset" about Chile's recent inflation trajectory, and said it could raise interest rates again over coming months.   \par \par \uc2 "This (inflation trajectory), obviously, upsets us deeply, and as such we are adopting monetary policy decisions to ensure that inflation returns to within the policy goal," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The bank raised its 2008 inflation outlook to 4.5 percent, from a previous estimate of 3.1 percent, which is far higher than its target range and above analysts' expectations.   \par \par \uc2 Its growth projections, down from a prior outlook for growth of 5.0 percent to 6.0 percent, were in line with the expected increase in gross domestic product for 2007 of 5.2 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Higher inflation has prompted a gradual rise in the benchmark interest rate to 6.25 percent in January from 4.0 percent a year ago.   \par \par \uc2 Chile's consumer price index jumped 7.8 percent in 2007, a 12-year high and up from a rate of 2.6 percent in 2006, driven mostly by higher fuel and food prices in the second half of the year.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a 12- to 24-month inflation target of 3 percent, with tolerance of plus or minus 1 percent.   \par \par \uc2 "The inflation projection ... indicates they're going to have to maintain a restrictive monetary policy in coming months," said Bertrand Delgado, an economist with IDEAglobal in New York.   \par \par \uc2 STRONG PESO, STRONG COPPER   \par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso has been trading near nine-year highs against the dollar this month, as rising interest rates in Chile and falling rates in the United States make the peso a more attractive investment option.   \par \par \uc2 "Even though the peso will be hit by global volatility and a U.S. economic slowdown, it will be supported by the interest rate differential," Delgado said.   \par \par \uc2 In the past, Chile's exporters have complained the strong peso depresses earnings and makes it difficult to compete in global markets, but De Gregorio said the bank saw no reason to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange rate.   \par \par \uc2 "When we have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , its been precisely because we've seen problems affecting the entire economy," De Gregorio told reporters. "If we haven't done anything, it's because we haven't seen these conditions."   \par \par \uc2 Average prices for copper, Chile's top export and economic mainstay, are expected to rise to $2.95/lb in 2008 from previous estimates of $2.70/lb.   \par \par \uc2 Such a rise would support an expected trade surplus of $16.4 billion in 2008, less than the record $24.5 billion surplus posted in 2007.   \par \par \uc2 "The trade balance is still positive," Delgado said. "And with economic growth at these levels, at around 5 percent, Chile is still pretty stable."   \par \par \uc2 Exports in 2008 are expected to come in at $68.3 billion, equal to the figure in 2007. (Additional reporting by Lisa Yulkowski; Writing by Pav Jordan; Editing by Diane Craft)   \par \par \uc2 CHILE-ECONOMY/OUTLOOK (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080116e41g0019l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
