\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Govt Holding $1.91B In New York BancoEstado Branch  \b0\par\par\uc2 455 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2006\par 18:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's government is holding $1.91 billion of its $4.19 billion in foreign reserves in time deposits and certificates of deposit at the New York City branch of state bank BancoEstado, Budget Director Alberto Arenas said Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Chile's government registered a 4.8% of gross domestic product budget surplus, in 2005, followed by a 2.2% surplus in the first quarter, amid surging earnings from state copper holdings and rising tax collections.  \par \par \uc2 As of April 30, "In consolidated terms, approximately...60% of the resources are invested outside the country," Arenas said.  \par \par \uc2 The Finance Ministry plans to report foreign investment data every quarter, amid pressure from many exporters to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 Surging prices for copper - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's principal export - and molybdenum have contributed to the peso strengthening against the dollar, to the chagrin of non-metallic exporters who have booked \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related losses.  \par \par \uc2 The previous and present governments have argued that they contribute to keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable by maintaining government dollar inflows related to the commodities boom off the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The holdings include those at BancoEstado in New York and at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where it has deposited $1.5 billion and thus kept them off the market, according to Arenas.  \par \par \uc2 Including the latter assets, the government is keeping 81.4% or $3.41 billion in dollar inflows away from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, while $779.44 million, or 18.6% of the assets, are invested in domestic instruments. [ 03-05-06 1627GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Arenas' report comes as the government seeks to move dollar earnings so non-metallic exporters don't suffer the consequences of copper's pull.  \par \par \uc2 Under the plan - announced Tuesday - budget surpluses above 1% of GDP will flow into an Economic and Social Stabilization Fund and into the government's pension reserve fund, up to certain limits specified in the legislation.  \par \par \uc2 If approved by congress, those funds in local or foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be invested in Chile or in foreign countries, in instruments specified by the pension system legislation, except shares.  \par \par \uc2 Up to 100% of the money could flow outside Chile.  \par \par \uc2 The flow of funds overseas could help insulate Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a greater extent from the volatility of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, according to supporters of the plan, which emulates Norway's similar efforts to deal with crude oil earnings.  \par \par \uc2 Chile could also seek third-party management of its foreign portfolio, which would be independently audited.  \par \par \uc2 Budget office Web site:  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dipres.cl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dipres.cl }}}\par \par \uc2 Finance Ministry Web site  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.hacienda.gov.cl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.hacienda.gov.cl }}}\par \par \uc2 -By Stephan Kueffner, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-460 8547; stephan.kueffner@dowjones.com [ 03-05-06 1639GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060503e253000vd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2