\par\par \b \uc2 Chilean peso closes at 7-week high against dollar  \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2006\par 16:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates with closing figures)  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Chile, Feb 21 (Reuters) - The Chilean peso rose nearly 1 percent on Tuesday to close at its strongest level against the dollar since Jan. 5, as banks exercised stop-loss orders after the peso broke through a 520-per-dollar resistance level, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <CHILJ> <CLP=CL>, advanced 0.81 percent to 518.50/519.00 per dollar compared with Monday's close at 522.70/523.20. It was the fifth session in a row of peso appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 "What is happening is that the conditions are there for the peso to continue appreciating. The market understood it that way and went out to stop losses, they went out to sell dollars to avoid bigger losses," a trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier in the session, the peso strengthened to more than 1 percent above Monday's close.  \par \par \uc2 Chile Finance Minister Nicolas Eyzaguirre said on Tuesday that the economy was set to expand by 5.5 percent to 6 percent in 2006 compared with last year, and said the government would have a third year in a row of budget surpluses this year.  \par \par \uc2 The peso shrugged off a weakening in the Brazilian real against the dollar on Tuesday <BRBY>, after shadowing the real's gains in recent sessions.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the 93rd time since October on Monday to shore up the flagging dollar, but the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has steadfastly maintained a hands-off policy toward \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -PESO (