\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Chile cenbank eyes peso measure only as exception  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Antonio de la Jara  \par \uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2006\par 15:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Recasts, adds byline, changes dateline)  \par \par \uc2  VALPARAISO, Chile, Jan 3 (Reuters) - Chile's powerful peso fell more than 1 percent on Tuesday as officials met with Congress to discuss exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market closed that it will only take measures in "exceptional situations."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Vittorio Corbo told Congress the autonomous body would keep an eye on the exchange rate, but reiterated there were no current plans to weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  "In such a case where the exchange rate were to evolve toward values which, in the opinion of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , differed significantly from fundamental determinants, be assured that we will use the tools that are at our disposition, particularly \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market," Corbo said.  \par \par \uc2  His statements came soon after \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets closed in Chile, and will likely disappoint traders who had bet the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would announce measures to weaken the peso, which has been free floating since 1999.  \par \par \uc2  The Chilean peso <CHILJ> <CLP=CL> fell 1.36 percent against the dollar to 520.30/520.80, its weakest in over a month. On Monday it closed at 513.20/513.70 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2  Chilean exporters in particular are calling for official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the strength of the peso after it gained 8.5 percent against the dollar in 2005, touching highs last seen in April 2000.  \par \par \uc2  Corbo said during a visit to Congress that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was keeping an eye on the exchange rate and reserved the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but had no plans to do so at the moment.  \par \par \uc2  "We are reaching (exchange rate) levels where one could worry and as such we are going to be monitoring every day," said Corbo, who also warned that any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be announced before hand.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy and its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are powering forward as prices for copper, the nation's top export, surge to new heights that even optimistic analysts had not expected.  \par \par \uc2  High copper prices are estimated to have brought in an additional $4 billion to the government in 2005 in profits from state copper miner Codelco, the world's largest producer of the red metal.  \par \par \uc2  An industrial group said on Monday that if the peso were to hold a value of 515/dollar in 2006, it would mean some $1 billion in lost revenues to exporters.  \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Nicolas Eyzaguirre, who joined Corbo on Tuesday's visit to the Chilean Congress in Valparaiso, said the peso strength was not yet at worrisome levels.  \par \par \uc2  He said the government was taking advantage of the strong peso to boost cheaper dollar assets and pay down debt.      \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-CHILE-PESO (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|D|M  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060103e213000q9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
