\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  would  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  if peso strength dangerous  \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Januar 2006\par 23:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Jan 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take measures if the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , supported by soaring prices for copper, appreciates "dangerously" against the dollar, Finance Minister Nicolas Eyzaguirre said on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The peso gained 8.5 percent against the dollar in 2005, touching highs last seen in April 2000, in large part because prices for copper, Chile's chief export, rose even beyond optimistic forecasts.  \par \par \uc2 Exporters of other goods have asked the government and the autonomous \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take measures to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "It is necessary to be permanently cautious that the price of the dollar go too much beyond what guarantees sustained growth in the future, for both exporters and for the economy as a whole," Eyzaguirre told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 "If authorities become convinced that the exchange rate is becoming dangerous, it will take the pertinent measures," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Chile has had a floating exchange rate policy since 1999.  \par \par \uc2 High copper prices are seen as having brought in an additional $4 billion to government coffers in 2005 as it received the profits of state copper miner Codelco, the world's largest producer of the red metal.  \par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <CHILJ> <CLP=CL> closed down 0.27 percent against the dollar to 513.20/513.70, compared with Friday's close at 511.80/512.30.  \par \par \uc2 An industrial group said on Monday that if the peso were to hold a value of 515/dollar in 2006, it would mean some $1 billion in lost revenues to exporters.  \par \par \uc2 On the other hand, Eyzaguirre also pointed out that the same exporters who are complaining today were not as quick to do so when the peso was trading at 760 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "So its not really fair to ask for help when prices are lower and take your winnings when things are going stupendously well and prices are higher."  \par \par \uc2 Eyzaguirre will join \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Vittorio Corbo in a special meeting with the senate on Tuesday to discuss the strength of the peso against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-CHILE-PESO|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060102e212000r0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
