\par\par \b \uc2 Chile central banker plays down strength of peso  \b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2005\par 19:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 VALPARAISO, Chile, Dec 20 (Reuters) - Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Vittorio Corbo on Tuesday played down the strength of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid concerns that the strong peso is harming exporters.  \par \par \uc2 Corbo said in a speech in Valparaiso, the coastal city that is home to Chile's Congress, that the peso's strength must be viewed relative to other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that have also fared well against a weaker dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "If you look at the dollar you should take some care. There is an optical illusion," Corbo said in a talk in the city about 140 km (87 miles) west of the capital.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar today is worth a lot less with respect to the peso, but its worth even less than that against the yen, the euro, and much less with respect to the Australian dollar and the New Zealand dollar."  \par \par \uc2 Chile's peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at close to 5 1/2-year highs against the dollar and many exporters complain it is taking a bite out of profits.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reiterated on several occasions that it has no plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-\b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -PESO|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051220e1ck001fv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
