\par\par \b \uc2 Chile stocks edge down as peso rises for a 7th day  \b0\par\par\uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2005\par 21:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Chile, Dec 6 (Reuters) - Chilean stocks edged down in mixed trade on Tuesday, as the peso shadowed the Brazilian real to rise for a seventh consecutive day to its highest level since April 2000.  \par \par \uc2 The IPSA blue-chip index <.IPSA> slipped 0.29 percent to 2,035.54 points while the broader IGPA index <.IGPA> was down 0.05 percent at 9,446.94, preliminary closing figures showed.  \par \par \uc2 "Volume wasn't bad today ... The exchange rate is obviously affecting the market," Euroamerica trader Jose Pablo Aguirre said.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the low dollar is hurting export companies that receive dollar income, such as major wood products manufacturer Masisa.  \par \par \uc2 Masisa , which sells its products in over 50 countries and has \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the U.S. and Mexico, was among the session's biggest decliners, as its stock retreated 2.87 percent to 104.90 pesos a share.  \par \par \uc2 Shipping company Sudamericana de Vapores was down 2.96 percent at 820 pesos a share. Vapores is Chile's largest container shipping firm.  \par \par \uc2 The retail sector, which imports large quantities of its merchandise, fared better, with leading department store chain Falabella rising 2.55 percent to 1,405 pesos a share and diversified retailer Cencosud jumping 3.0 percent to 1,030 pesos a share.  \par \par \uc2 "Cencosud has been incredible, it was about a quarter of what we traded today," said Aguirre.  \par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market the Chilean peso <CHILJ> <CLP=CL> rose 0.63 percent to close at 510.30/510.80 per dollar, compared to Monday's close at 513.50/514.00.  \par \par \uc2 "Market activity is down drastically for year-end, so today's rise in the peso is closely tied to the (Brazilian) real," a trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The real, rising on increased export sector revenues, continued its advance despite strong sales of dollar indexed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts by Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks to stop the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall.  \par \par \uc2 The peso has risen 12 percent against the dollar in the second half of the year and many exporters complain that the strong peso is taking a bite out of profits. However, the government has said several times that it will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -STOCKS|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051206e1c60020j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
