\par\par \b \uc2 Chilean stocks retreat, peso rises for 6th session  \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2005\par 22:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Chile, Dec 5 (Reuters) - Chilean stocks retreated on Monday after lower-than-expected economic data, while high copper prices pushed the peso up for a sixth straight session against the dollar to a fresh 5-1/2-year high.  \par \par \uc2 The IPSA blue-chip index <.IPSA> slipped 0.75 percent to 2,041.44 points while the broader IGPA index <.IGPA> fell 0.60 percent to 9,451.71, preliminary closing figures showed.  \par \par \uc2 "The economic activity figures are below projections, and the market's interpretation of the data isn't good," said Rodrigo Sarria, deputy manager of the Intervalores brokerage.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued its monthly economic activity report, showing growth for October at 4.9 percent compared to October 2004, less than the median 5.3 percent median projection of analysts in a Reuters poll.  \par \par \uc2 Diversified retailer Cencosud led blue-chip declines as its shares slumped 3.71 percent to 999.80 pesos a share, its lowest close in almost five months, in heavy trading.  \par \par \uc2 Other leading decliners included wood products manufacturer Masisa , which is seeking to raise $160 million in a share offering. Masisa stock fell 3.32 percent to 108 pesos.  \par \par \uc2 Shares of power generator Colbun were down 2.79 percent to 69.99 pesos a share.  \par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market the Chilean peso <CHILJ> <CLP=CL> inched up 0.1 percent to close at 513.50/514.00 per dollar compared to Friday's close at 514.00/514.50.  \par \par \uc2 "With copper as high as it is and with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the dollar's descent, investors have continued to unload dollars," a trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Some Chilean exporters have asked the government to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the peso's rise against the dollar, but officials have insisted that they will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless there are signs of market speculation.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -STOCKS|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051205e1c5001yx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
