\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Central Banker Says Not Readying Peso  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2005\par 17:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso's rally to its strongest level in five and a half years against the dollar hasn't set the alarm bells ringing at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vice president said Monday.  \par \par \uc2 "We've got a flexible exchange rate policy where under special circumstances we could find an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  necessary, but that situation hasn't occurred," said Jose de Gregorio at a meeting with business leaders.  \par \par \uc2 The bank has threatened to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in the past three years as the peso plunged to all-time lows against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but in the end provided dollar liquidity in the bond market without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly.  \par \par \uc2 Since then, the peso has gradually strengthened in line with other commodities-based and Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . So far this year, it has strengthened some 6.5% against the greenback to 527.20 pesos to the dollar from CLP561.50 Jan. 3.  \par \par \uc2 While government officials have said the peso's gains stem from fundamentals, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has limited itself to saying that it could call an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the event of major speculation.  \par \par \uc2 Some economists say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserve holdings, which have dropped in recent months, don't adequately reflect the surge in foreign trade, which has reached record highs.  \par \par \uc2 De Gregorio said the bank's net position in dollars hasn't changed and that the drop in reserves also reflects the strengthening of the dollar against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  the bank also holds in its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  portfolio.  \par \par \uc2 At the same time, the bank in August said it planned to sell assets in dollars and other foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  worth $1.47 billion through the end of the year.  \par \par \uc2 Wednesday, the bank will report third-quarter gross domestic product growth. Weaker-than-expected mining output limited growth in the third quarter, but overall GDP growth remains on target with the bank's 6.0%-6.5% estimate for the year.  \par \par \uc2 Last year, GDP growth came in at 6.1%. Last week, the Finance Ministry estimated that GDP grew 5.3% on the year in the third quarter, while domestic demand grew more than 10%.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Web site  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bcentral.cl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.bcentral.cl }}}\par \par \uc2 -By Patricia San Juan, Dow Jones Newswires; +562-460-8547; patty.sanjuan@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (Stephan Kueffner contributed to this report) [ 21-11-05 1618GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051121e1bl000t8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
