\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends Stronger But Some Worry About  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2005\par 19:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso ended slightly stronger against the dollar Thursday, in line with the euro and Brazilian real, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 However, some worry that the peso's rally - it has reached its highest level since mid-2000 in recent sessions - could spark \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the surge doesn't run out of steam, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP524.40 to the dollar from CLP524.80 Wednesday, after trading in a CLP522.40-CLP524.90 range.  \par \par \uc2 According to Chile's Banco Central, the peso traded at CLP523.01 to the dollar around 1500 GMT, about an hour before the market closed.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real opened marginally stronger Thursday after Finance Minister Antonio Palocci dispelled rumors that he would resign and mounted a spirited defense of the government's austere economic policies in testimony before a senate committee.  \par \par \uc2 The peso often trades in the same direction as the euro and real. The latter is also a key indicator of short-term confidence in the region.  \par \par \uc2 The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't hold on to early gains as the market began to worry the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might take action, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 On two previous occasions in recent years, the bank has threatened multi-billion dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  following plunges in the peso, along with providing dollar-indexed bonds.  \par \par \uc2 The bank doesn't pursue an exchange-rate target, but says it can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the event of major speculative imbalances.  \par \par \uc2 The peso still has room to near CLP519 ahead of major technical resistance.  \par \par \uc2 On the local bond market, rates rose on a rise in supply sparked by a likely slowdown in inflation for next month in line with a drop in fuel prices.  \par \par \uc2 Bond rates are adjusted for inflation so that a lower inflation outlook makes bonds a less attractive investment.  \par \par \uc2 The yield on the inflation-indexed eight-year PRCs closed at 3.37%, up from 3.20% Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 At the long end of the curve, the yield on the 20-year PRC closed at 3.50%, up from 3.33% Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Patricia San Juan, Dow Jones Newswires; +56-2-460-8546; chile@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (Stephan Kueffner contributed to this report.) [ 17-11-05 1827GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1170 1844  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051117e1bh0013u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
