\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Again Ends Weaker On Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2004\par 18:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso again closed weaker against the dollar Tuesday, in reaction to the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's second consecutive daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, according to traders.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at CLP583.00 to the dollar, weaker than its CLP581.75 close Monday, after trading in a broad CLP578.40-583.70 range.  \par \par \uc2 The peso opened stronger, at CLP579.80, and quickly weakened after the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  made "modest" dollar purchases, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The Andean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  often trades in sync with its Brazilian counterpart. The real also often plays a key role in peso trading as the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an important short-term indicator of investor confidence in Latin America.  \par \par \uc2 In addition, the peso also weakened in reaction to banks squaring positions ahead of Wednesday's Immaculate Conception holiday.  \par \par \uc2 In the local bond market, the benchmark peso-denominated, inflation-indexed, eight-year PRC closed at a yield of 2.75%, compared with 2.76% Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Rates held fairly steady amid thin activity ahead of Thursday's monthly \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary policy meeting, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Markets expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise the benchmark interest rate 25 basis points to 2.50%.  \par \par \uc2 The 20-year PRC closed at a yield of 3.32% unchanged from Monday.  \par \par \uc2 All financial markets will be closed Wednesday in observance of the Day of the Immaculate Conception. Trading will resume Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; +56 2 460 8544 carolina.pica@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (Patricia San Juan contributed to this report.) [ 07-12-04 1726GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1170 1844  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041207e0c7000vu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
