\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends Weaker On Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2004\par 21:04\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2004, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Dec 06, 2004 (ODC via COMTEX) --  \par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso closed weaker against the dollar Monday, in reaction to the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, according to traders. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at CLP581.75 to the dollar, weaker than its CLP579.60 close Friday, after trading in a broad CLP577.50-583.20 range. The peso opened stronger, at CLP579.00, and quickly weakened on a European bank's dollar purchases. It then continued sliding after the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  made a "modest," by traders' estimates, greenback buy. The Andean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  often trades in sync with its Brazilian counterpart. The real also often plays a key role in peso trading as the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an important short-term indicator of investor confidence in Latin America. In addition, the peso reacted to copper prices falling for the fifth-consecutive session. Chile is world's largest copper producer, accounting for 30% of global output. Falling copper prices reduce export revenue inflows to the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, traders said. In the local bond market, the benchmark peso-denominated, inflation-indexed, eight-year PRC closed at a yield of 2.76%, compared with 2.67% Friday. Rates rose in line with market expectations of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  25-basis-point interest rate hike, to 2.50%, at its monthly monetary policy meeting scheduled for Thursday. The 20-year PRC closed at a yield of 3.32%, compared with 3.30% Friday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; +56 2 460 8544 carolina.pica@dowjones.com (Patricia San Juan contributed to this report)  \par \par \uc2 Copyright 2004 Dow Jones. All rights reserved.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020041206e0c6005cg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
