\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends Near Support On Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fear  \b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2004\par 18:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso weakened against the dollar Monday as the market started to worry that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might intervere on behalf of the punished U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at CLP562.00 to the dollar, near technical support and 0.8% weaker than the CLP557.80 close Friday, after trading in a CLP557.00-562.30 range.  \par \par \uc2 Technical resistance stands at CLP556.30, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Late Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lopped another 50 basis points off its key interest rate to 1.75% from 2.25%, a previously record-low rate, surprising the market.  \par \par \uc2 While the peso shrugged off the cut in Friday's trading, dollar demand rose following comments by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet, who earlier Monday gave the clearest signal yet that euro-zone policymakers are growing increasingly concerned about the strength of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and won't sit on their hands indefinitely.  \par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  however has so far said it is unconcerned with the strengthening of the peso. In recent history - when the peso swiftly plunged to record lows versus the dollar in late 2001 and 2002 - the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fired a warning shot in announcing it was willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by providing dollar liquidity to the market via dollar-issued bonds.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't target the peso as such, but it has left the door open in the event of an emergency, as when the peso plunged to record lows ahead of the Argentina crisis and the Iraq war.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts have said the bank might soon accelerate buybacks of the bonds to take back the liquidity.  \par \par \uc2 Along with other commodity-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso has appreciated sharply in recent months, helped primarily by the rise in copper prices and a positive outlook for the Chilean economy. It has also latched onto the euro amid the global weakening of the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 -By Stephan Kueffner, Dow Jones Newswires; 562-460-8546; stephan.kueffner@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 1170 1844  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040112e01c000st\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
