\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Fin Min Worried Peso Could Spark Short-Term Flows  \b0\par\par\uc2 480 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2003\par 23:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chilean Finance Minister Nicolas Eyzaguirre Monday said the peso's sharp appreciation against the dollar might spark detrimental short-term speculative \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows.  \par \par \uc2 "When the peso strengthens as a result of very good prospects for the economy, there's nothing to be done. But if there's speculative pressure, one has to think where it's coming from, and that can be deactivated if you move on the factors that could be producing the speculation," Eyzaguirre said during a briefing at the finance ministry.  \par \par \uc2 The peso has appreciated sharply in recent months, helped primarily by the rise in copper prices and a positive outlook for the Chilean economy.  \par \par \uc2 Chile is the world's largest copper producer, and the peso continued to benefit from high copper prices Monday, traders said, reaching its strongest level in 32 months by closing at CLP596.80 to the dollar. For every cent copper rises in world markets, Chile receives an additional $100 million in dollar inflows.  \par \par \uc2 As recently as March, the peso traded near record weakness around CLP760 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 There's no evidence yet of a massive entry of speculative capital into the Andean country, but Eyzaguirre called on the financial system to make sure that institutions as well as debtors are duly covered in their dollar and peso positions in order to avoid any future imbalances.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the most recent spike - following a surprise \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate cut Thursday - has unsettled the market, leading to fewer transactions, they added.  \par \par \uc2 The peso is, therefore, unlikely to quickly strengthen further and will move in a tight CLP595-CLP600 range in the coming sessions, they also said.  \par \par \uc2 Still, Eyzaguirre's statements are the first warnings regarding the risks of overshooting on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since it started its rally. \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  only in the face of severe imbalances, has so far said it's unconcerned by the peso's recovery.  \par \par \uc2 However, the rally has contributed to a fall in inflation to well below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's minimum 2% target, leading the bank to surprisingly cut its prime interest rate by 50 basis points to 2.25% annually last Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The rally has been based on fundamental factors such as exports and an improved outlook for the domestic economy, and the government won't cut back on spending to undermine the peso. That would negatively impact domestic spending which is still recovering from a prolonged slump, Eyzaguirre said.  \par \par \uc2 He also ruled out increasing spending as that would undermine Chile's investment-grade status, he added.  \par \par \uc2 Chile is the only investment-grade country in South America.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Ministry Web site:  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.minhda.cl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.minhda.cl}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Stephan Kueffner, Dow Jones Newswires; 562-460-8546; stephan.kueffner@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (Patricia San Juan contributed to this article.)  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031215dzcf000xv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
