\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Central Bank \highlight\uc2  rules out  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2003\par 17:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to slow down appreciation of the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  , which has gained 11.5 percent against the U.S. dollar this year and hit a 27-month high last week.  \par \par \uc2 Market traders have come to expect some sort of \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to defend the powerful exporting sector, which complains the strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will dig into their returns.  \par \par \uc2 "Its hard to imagine that we have a fragile exchange rate ... We have a flexible exchange rate and we have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exceptional cases in case of short-term turbulence but today we are very far from that situation," Jose de Gregorio, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member who was speaking for the bank, told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has floated the peso since 1999, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  sporadically to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during times of turbulence such as the Argentine devaluation and Brazil's financial crisis last year.  \par \par \uc2 "We have to let the market function adequately in situations that are relatively normal," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The peso gained 5.5 percent against the dollar in the third quarter and traded at 638.80/639.30 at mid-session on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 De Gregorio said the strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  favored prices of copper, Chile's top export, and was a natural reaction to an upbeat economic outlook for Chile.  \par \par \uc2 "The weakness of the dollar is an international phenomenon and responds also to a more auspicious economic outlook internally, especially much better prices for our goods, which we have seen in the price of copper," De Gregorio said.  \par \par \uc2 De Gregorio estimated that for every 1 percent depreciation of the dollar against major world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , copper prices would rise 0.8 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "The same occurs with prices of all raw materials," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031028dzas003cc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
