\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk Drops  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Threat Despite Low Peso \b0\par\par\uc2  By Stephan Kueffner \par \uc2 759 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2003\par 17:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO -(Dow Jones)- Despite the Chilean peso's weakness, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has given the market a clear signal it won't move to prop it up at this time. \par \par \uc2  In its latest debt calendar, published on its web site over the weekend, the bank sharply cut back its issuance of dollar-denominated debt, or BCDs, to just $60 million a month, from $240 million. Meanwhile, an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threat uttered four months ago has run out without being replaced. \par \par \uc2  "Those $2 billion are no longer available," a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokeswoman said, referring to the amount that had been earmarked for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Initial market response was measured, with a slight drop from the previous session's close. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed Monday at CLP743.50 per dollar, compared to CLP742.30 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "While the (dollar) exchange rate is very high, it's fully justifiable due to the Iraq war fear and the rise in crude oil prices. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is reconfirming that it will act only when the dollar has an unjustified rise and this is consistent with ... not going out to fight the market," said economist Cristian Gardeweg at Santander Investment. \par \par \uc2  Dollar-denominated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds provide greenback liquidity to holders, underpinning the peso in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The peso has suffered since late December, mainly from the rise in crude oil prices brought on by the twin crises in oil-rich Iraq and Venezuela. \par \par \uc2  Early October, the peso hit a record low of CLP760.80 to the dollar, hit by high oil prices in the wake of the U.S.-Iraq crisis and the decline of the Brazilian real, which reflected the loss of investor confidence in Latin American economies. \par \par \uc2  It recovered after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called the fall "to some degree a market overreaction" and said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with up to $2 billion of the country's foreign reserves over four months and offer up to $2 billion in BCDs with two- to five-year maturities. \par \par \uc2  After the announcement, the peso swiftly won back close to 10% from the dollar and traded under CLP700, while Brazil won a honeymoon with the markets and without any direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Then the threat of war in Iraq became more acute and Venezuela's general strike erupted on the scene. \par \par \uc2  That pulled the peso back down again to levels around CLP745. It was kept from falling further by fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  Now, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is guarding its hand, while "the market is screaming for a greater amount (of issuance), proven by the last auctions of BCDs in which demand has been far greater than the offer," said trader Cristian Donoso at brokerage Banchile. \par \par \uc2  As the peso recovered, demand for BCDs dropped and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut back supply, but as the oil producers' crises continued, bid levels increased sharply, but retreated slightly at the last auctions Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In the end, it auctioned only $1.4 billion out of the $2.0 billion it had earmarked. \par \par \uc2  The future monthly $60 million is low considering the peso's rate and the market's hedging needs, "but the market is long on dollars and that could slow peso depreciation," Donoso said. \par \par \uc2  A lot will depend on how successful major companies were in hedging over the past months, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Should they find themselves in need of dollars in the near future, they'll be forced into the market, particularly if they feel the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't worried about a major drop in the peso, they added. \par \par \uc2  That might be the case. In its monetary policy report issued Jan. 15, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said any effect from the high oil prices would be transitional, with inflation dropping by the end of the year. Additionally, data released this year has shown headline and core inflation well under control and easily within the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2%-4% target range. \par \par \uc2  As a result of earlier issuance maturing in the last third of this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will after July begin raising the auction amounts, including two- and five-year bonds, it said Friday. \par \par \uc2  Bondholders from March onward will be able to switch their bonds to new two-year bonds at market conditions six months before maturity, the bank added. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Web site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bcentral.cl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.bcentral.cl}}}\par \par \uc2  -By Stephan Kueffner, Dow Jones Newswires; 562-460-8546; stephan.kueffner@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030210dz2a00118\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picsc