\par\par \b \uc2  Chile Peso Ends Dn In Range Trading As Brazil Real Slumps \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2002\par 18:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO -(Dow Jones)- Chile's peso closed lower against the dollar Tuesday in range trading, hit by profit-taking that sent the Brazilian real lower. \par \par \uc2  The peso finished at CLP720.50 to the dollar, from CLP719.00 Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The peso was pulled down by a more negative international environment," a Santiago trader said, pointing to the decline in the Brazilian real. \par \par \uc2  However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's auction of $60 million in dollar-denominated bonds during the session - which met very strong demand - mitigated the fall by providing liquidity to the market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Trading was also limited because of the absence of corporate players in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, which imposed range trading between the banks, they added. \par \par \uc2  As a result, the peso failed to break in a sustained way the technical resistance mark of its old historic low of CLP718.60, set a year ago ahead of Argentina's economic and financial meltdown. \par \par \uc2  However, it has regained some 6% since \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market because it considered the peso's swift fall below CLP760 a month ago unjustified. \par \par \uc2  A sustained rise above CLP718 could trigger a return to prices of around CLP700 to the dollar in the near term, traders have said. \par \par \uc2  Also domestically, inflation for October came in surprisingly high, up 0.9% against an expected 0.5%, ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest-rate decision Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Stephan Kueffner, Dow Jones Newswires; 562-460-8546; stephan.kueffner@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (Patricia San Juan contributed to this report.) \par \par \uc2  1170 1844 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021105dyb50013f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
