\par\par \b \uc2  Chile Peso Ends Up, With Room To Rise; Focus On Brazil \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2002\par 18:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO -(Dow Jones)- Chile's peso closed higher against the dollar Monday, boosted by the Brazilian real's continuing recovery and rising share prices world wide. Depending on how Brazil fares, the peso could gain sharply in the near term, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The peso finished at CLP719.00 to the dollar, from CLP726.20 Thursday, the last day of trading due to a public holiday Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Improved perspectives for Brazil and the rise of most international bourses have created a felling of more optimisim regarding the external panorama," a Santiago trader said, referring to the impact of leftist Brazilian President-elect Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva. \par \par \uc2  Banks are letting go of dollars they had hoarded to confront a possible financial crisis in the region, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Lula's ascent to the presidency was accompanied by a financial crisis and loss of confidence in Brazil, leading to the International Monetary Fund's biggest bailout ever and sharp falls in the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Chilean peso, as investors turned elsewhere. \par \par \uc2  In intraday trading, the peso failed to sustainedly break the technical resistance mark of its old historic low of CLP718.60, set a year ago ahead of Argentina's economic and financial meltdown. \par \par \uc2  However, it has regained some 6% since \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market because it considered the peso's swift fall unjustified. \par \par \uc2  A sustained rise above CLP718 could trigger a return to prices of around CLP700 to the dollar in the near term, traders said. \par \par \uc2  However, that will also depend on how successful Brazil is at rolling over debt in the near term, they added. \par \par \uc2  -By Stephan Kueffner, Dow Jones Newswires; 562-460-8546; stephan.kueffner@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (Patricia San Juan contributed to this report) \par \par \uc2  1170 1844 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021104dyb4000za\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
