\par\par \b \uc2  Chile Fin Min:To Miss Growth Target Won't Mean Major Debt \b0\par\par\uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2002\par 22:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO -(Dow Jones)- Chile won't have to resort to major new debt to finance its budget next year if it fails to grow the 4.0% the government expects, Chilean Finance Minister Nicolas Eyzaguirre said Monday. \par \par \uc2  "A missed percentage point in gross domestic product growth will lead to only 0.2% more in debt, so if we grow only 3%, debt will rise to just 0.9% of GDP, and if we grow just 2%, it will rise to just 1.1%, against 0.7%" currently projected, Eyzaguirre said during a press briefing. \par \par \uc2  Chile plans a new bond issuance next year, but Eyzaguirre wouldn't specify an amount of issuance or expected spreads to Treasurys. \par \par \uc2  However, because of the small weight of Chilean debt in overall emerging debt markets, the amount of new bonds will have little impact on current spreads of Chilean sovereign debt, Eyzaguirre said. \par \par \uc2  "In the medium term of 12 to 24 months, I expect spreads to narrow" versus Treasurys, once uncertainty regarding conflict between the U.S. and Iraq and Brazil's public finance ease, he added. \par \par \uc2  While Chilean debt is more expensive than that of its Latin American neighbors, it is cheaper than that of eastern European countries with worse macroeconomic fundamentals than Chile, but more closely tied to the European Union, he also said. \par \par \uc2  Last Friday, Eyzaguirre presented additional debt data to respond to domestic criticism regarding the level of foreign debt owed by the government, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and state-owned companies. \par \par \uc2  Eyzaguirre on Monday said foreign bondholders hadn't sought additional information from Chile on its debt, and that the International Monetary Fund also separately lists central government, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and public company debt. \par \par \uc2  Chile has managed to keep its economy growing despite economic depression in neighboring Argentina and crises in several Latin American countries, but growth rates are far below levels seen in the 1990s, and unemployment remains stubbornly high at just under 10%. \par \par \uc2  "This year, Latin America's growth will be around minus 1%, falling for the first time since the early Eighties, while Chile will grow around 2%. There's no crisis symptoms here. Last time around (during the Pinochet military dictatorship), we led the region in falling," Eyzaguirre said. \par \par \uc2  Regarding the likely electoral victory of leftist Brazilian presidential candidate Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, which sparked a financial crisis during the campaign, Eyzaguirre said Chile could be hit by a fall in exports to Brazil and a drop in the value of Chilean assets there. \par \par \uc2  Runoff elections in Brazil will take place Sunday. \par \par \uc2  Most fundamentally, fear of Lula has been reducing foreign direct investment in the region, including Chile. \par \par \uc2  To avoid further problems, a recovery of Brazil is fundamentally necessary, but Lula's team includes respected economists, and he could manage to restore credibility during the "honeymoon" at the beginning of his term, Eyzaguirre said. \par \par \uc2  He added Chile's peso has managed to decouple from the Brazilian real. Both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to record lows against the dollar during Lula's campaign, but the peso has recovered slightly after \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  threatened to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Finance Ministry Web site {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.minhda.cl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.minhda.cl}}}\par \par \uc2  -By Stephan Kueffner, Dow Jones Newswires; 562-460-8546; stephan.kueffner@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021021dyal0019b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
