\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2 's Peso Recovers From Historic Low On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 449 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2002\par 19:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso closed higher Friday, rising from a historic minimum against the dollar after Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned the market it could use up to $4 billion to supply liquidity in the next few months. \par \par \uc2  The peso finished Friday at CLP747.20 to the dollar, from CLP760.50 on Thursday. Its Thursday intraday all-time low was CLP760.80 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Despite the recovery, the market is still short on dollars, hence the peso couldn't hold at the CLP739.50 intraday high it reached shortly after trading began, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement hasn't yet lead to an influx of dollars into the market," a Santiago trader said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Thursday said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a total of up to $2 billion in dollar-denominated "BCD" bonds and $2 billion in cash to support the sagging local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Uncertainty surrounding Brazil's presidential elections and doubts about that country's ability to meet its debt-financing needs have been affecting markets across the region. The situation is likely to remain volatile as the crisis in confidence affecting Brazil could limit its ability to roll over debt due ahead of the Oct. 27 presidential runoff. \par \par \uc2  Considering the uncertainty, its unlikely the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will risk \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  below CLP750 to the dollar, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's political situation has been weighing on markets for months because of the popularity of leftist candidate Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, who appears poised to win the presidency. \par \par \uc2  The peso has also been hit by the combination of low copper and high oil prices. \par \par \uc2  While the sluggish global economy has lessened demand for copper, Chile's prime export dollar earner, the U.S.-Iraq crisis has pushed oil prices up, which is detrimental to Chile's terms of trade as the country imports much of its oil. \par \par \uc2  Additionally, the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hesitancy to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  has undermined the peso, traders have said. The peso has lost nearly 15% of its value this year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had earlier said the peso's fall was justified by economic fundamentals and that it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only under exceptional circumstances. \par \par \uc2  In its statement late Thursday, it said that "Part of the depreciation observed recently reflects movements in a market that has operated with little liquidity and high volatility, and, therefore, overreacting to some degree." \par \par \uc2  Chile's foreign reserves have been relatively stable this year, in the $14.50-15.20 billion range. \par \par \uc2  -By Stephan Kueffner, Dow Jones Newswires; 562-460-8546; stephan.kueffner@dowjones.com (Patricia San Juan contributed to this report) \par \par \uc2  1170 1844 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021011dyab0011r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
