\par\par \b \uc2  Chile stocks firm on bargain hunting. \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2002\par 00:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, Chile, Oct 11 (Reuters) - Chile's stocks chirped slightly higher on Friday on bargain hunting despite roaring gains on Wall Street and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's promise to inject $4 billion dollars into the struggling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The IPSA blue-chip index rose 0.82 percent to 76.94 points, while the wider index gained 0.25 percent to 4,621.86 points. \par \par \uc2  U.S. stocks surged on Friday on new found optimism over earnings outlooks. \par \par \uc2  "Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market which is beneficial for companies with debts in dollars, investors are still keeping their distance from the bourse due to the domestic and regional uncertainty," said Eliodoro Suarez, trader with Chilemarket brokerage. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said late on Thursday it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the peso by placing dollar bonds of up to $2 billion in the market over the next four months and selling $2 billion in international reserves on the market when it sees necessary. \par \par \uc2  Investors fear leftist candidate Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva is likely to win presidential elections on Oct. 27 and may mismanage the economy. Brazilian markets are seen as a benchmark for Latin America. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the only gains in the local market were as a result of some purchases of ADRs at bargain prices, though the volumes were minimal. \par \par \uc2  Telecoms leader Telefonica CTC Chile surged 2.56 percent to 1,600 pesos while electric energy company Endesa Chile leapt 1.8 percent to 162 pesos. \par \par \uc2  Supermarket group D&S gained 2.31 percent to settle at 399 pesos. \par \par \uc2  Trading volumes were low at 4.574 billion pesos ($6.1 million). \par \par \uc2  ($1 = 747 pesos). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021011dyab016ft\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
