\par\par \b \uc2  Chile's Peso Ends Higher As Foreign Dollars Come Back \b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2002\par 20:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO -(Dow Jones)- Chile's peso closed higher as foreign banks and brokerages put dollars back on to the local market, helped by the recovery in world stock markets and the Brazilian real. \par \par \uc2  The peso ended at CLP745.50 to the dollar, from CLP748.80 Monday, trading in a tight range. \par \par \uc2  "It looks like the market has accepted the CLP750 floor. Whenever the market gets close to it, profit-taking sets in," a Santiago trader said. \par \par \uc2  Monday, the peso set an intraday all-time low of CLP752.20. \par \par \uc2  The peso has fallen to historic lows on international uncertainty, with Brazil in the foreground due to the popularity of a leftist presidential candidate in pre-election polls there. \par \par \uc2  The real's fall has reflected the withdrawal of dollars from the region, including Chile. \par \par \uc2  However, the real recovered Tuesday, helped by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions and trade data, propping up the peso. \par \par \uc2  Still, in the few days ahead of the Oct. 6 elections in Brazil, the market could cautiously test new lows, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Speaking in New York, Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Carlos Massad continued to tread a fine line regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reminding the market of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's large dollar reserves but saying decoupling of the peso from other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' moves would be necessary before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps in. \par \par \uc2  "We are looking closely at what's going on with the peso rate," said Massad, adding that the bank's international reserves, at around $15 billion, are available to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if necessary. \par \par \uc2  But he also suggested that he wasn't overly concerned with the current exchange rate, and that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would require more than the peso weakening only against the greenback, given the country's diversified export markets. \par \par \uc2  "For \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be justified, we have to consider that the situation is extraordinary, that is, that the peso is not moving with the rest of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but that it has taken a loss by itself," said Massad, adding that this hasn't been the case until now. \par \par \uc2  The peso has also fallen due to higher crude oil prices because of fears of a war between the U.S. and Iraq and low prices for copper, Chile's principal dollar earner. \par \par \uc2  -By Stephan Kueffner, Dow Jones Newswires; 562-460-8546; stephan.kueffner@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1170 1844 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021001dya10013u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
