\par\par \b \uc2  Big peso drop may spur  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  CenBank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hugh Bronstein \par \uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2002\par 18:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Oct 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  is well positioned to withstand the current global economic turbulence but its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the peso weakens more dramatically than the swooning \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of other Latin American nations, the bank's governor said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The peso hit historic lows on Monday amid fears that neighboring Brazil may be about to elect a president who will frighten investors away from the region. If the peso starts to fall independently of the regional weakness, which has hit not only Brazil but Mexico, Carlos Massad told a group of Wall Street analysts that the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may step in to buy the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "For \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be justified, we have to consider the situation to be extraordinary, that the peso is not moving with the rest of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but that it is taking a loss by itself," Massad told a meeting hosted by the Americas Society. \par \par \uc2  "In that case, we would feel justified to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The Chilean peso strengthened slightly on Tuesday, following an uptick in Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real . The peso gained 0.17 percent at midday to 747.50/747.80 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  be necessary, Massad said the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be announced publicly. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the second half of 2001 to prop up a peso hit by fallout from Argentina's deep financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  Chilean interest rates are at historic lows as the country tries to continue growing in the face of a listless global economy that has depressed the price of the nation's main export, copper. \par \par \uc2  Analysts wonder if the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can continue lowering rates, given the peso's weakness. \par \par \uc2  "We do not discard the possibility of future action on interest rates either way, downward or upward, depending on the general conditions," Massad said. \par \par \uc2  Massad said he expects the country's inflation rate to be around 3 percent by the end of the year "unless oil prices shoot up substantially as a result of a war in the Middle East." \par \par \uc2  The threat of a U.S. attack on Iraq has jacked up oil prices, which places a burden on energy importers, such as Chile, while weighing on global equity markets. This atmosphere of fear has prompted a flight from risky emerging market assets and toward safe-haven U.S. Treasury bonds. \par \par \uc2  But Massad, citing Chile's strong export sector, urged his audience to discriminate among Latin American countries, saying that the economic problems of some should not be seen contaminating the whole region. \par \par \uc2  "We are in a position to continue growing despite the difficulties around us," said Massad, who predicted Chile's gross domestic product will expand by 2 percent to 2.5 percent this year. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021001dya100x6u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
