\par\par \b \uc2  Chile's Peso Ends Lower On Real, Seen Testing New Lows \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2002\par 20:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO -(Dow Jones)- Chile's peso closed slightly lower Monday, dragged down by the Brazilian real's renewed fall to a record low. \par \par \uc2  As a result of the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's woes, the peso could also continue testing new record lows, though a major drop is unlikely, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The peso ended at CLP748.80 to the dollar Monday, from CLP744.20 Friday. \par \par \uc2  It set an intraday all-time low of CLP752.20, marginally lower than the previous CLP752.00 it fell to Friday, also in intraday trading. \par \par \uc2  In the third quarter, the peso at closing fell to CLP748.80 from CLP691.40, a drop of 8.3%. \par \par \uc2  The international uncertainty that has sent the peso to historic lows continued to weigh on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, with Brazil in the foreground due to the popularity of a leftist presidential candidate in pre-election polls there. \par \par \uc2  The real's fall has reflected the withdrawal of dollars from the region, including Chile. \par \par \uc2  The peso has also fallen due to higher crude oil prices because of fears of a war between the U.S. and Iraq. \par \par \uc2  Low prices for copper, Chile's principal dollar earner, and the global fall of stock market prices, above all in European equities, also weighed on the peso, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stabilized after hawkish signals from Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  In Chile, market participants continue to see the CLP750.00 level as a solid bottom beyond which \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they added. \par \par \uc2  "The market's still working with the CLP750 level, with banks taking profits beyond that since there's fear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might take measures to brake the drop," a Santiago trader said. \par \par \uc2  Still, in the few days ahead of the Oct. 6 elections in Brazil, the market could cautiously test new lows, traders said. \par \par \uc2  -By Stephan Kueffner, Dow Jones Newswires; 562-460-8546; stephan.kueffner@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1170 1844 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020930dy9u0019l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
