\par\par \b \uc2  Chile Finance Minister: Peso Fall To Lows `Exaggerated' \b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2002\par 19:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO -(Dow Jones)- The Chilean peso's fall to new lows Monday was "exaggerated," Chilean Finance Minister Nicolas Eyzaguirre said Monday. \par \par \uc2  Hit by higher crude oil prices due to fears of a war between the U.S. and Iraq, as well as a fall in the Brazilian real due to the popularity of a leftist presidential candidate in pre-election polls, the peso hit an intraday low of CLP750.80 earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  However, "the price of the dollar is currently exaggerated and doesn't have anything to do with the fundamentals of the Chilean economy," Eyzaguirre told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The fall won't have a lasting effect on the economy and significantly raise inflation, he added. \par \par \uc2  Mid-term interest rates haven't risen and Chile's country-risk indicators have declined, demonstrating that the economy isn't worried about inflation and that there are no risks to stability, he said. \par \par \uc2  "Interest rates continue absolutely unchanged, which is what's important from the point of view of reactivating the economy," he said, adding that he expects the peso to return to equilibrium levels. \par \par \uc2  Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has linked the peso's recent plunge to declining prices in copper, Chile's main export, as well as oil prices and developments in the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It has also ruled out direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as long as the peso's fall is driven by market fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Eyzaguirre said a decision on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be left to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone. \par \par \uc2  Regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2003 budget, Eyzaguirre said the deficit would likely be lower than the 1% of gross domestic product estimated for this year. \par \par \uc2  The government is due to introduce next year's budget package in congress before the end of the month. \par \par \uc2  -By Stephan Kueffner, Dow Jones Newswires; (562) 460-8546; stephan.kueffner@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020923dy9n0011p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
