\par\par \b \uc2  Chile's Peso Ends Lower On Low Copper, High Oil Prices \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2002\par 19:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO -(Dow Jones)- Chile's peso ended slightly lower Friday, again hit by the combination of low copper prices and high oil prices but held above its all-time low against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Copper is Chile's principal export, while it imports much of its oil. \par \par \uc2  The peso closed at CLP715.90 to the dollar, from CLP715.70 Thursday, but after volatile trading in which it once again risked breaching its all-time low of CLP718.70. \par \par \uc2  It hit that low last October, but came dangerously close to breaking it last week and over the past three sessions. \par \par \uc2  Friday's intraday low was CLP718.10. \par \par \uc2  The peso started lower again as copper fell on fears of sluggish economic growth, while the U.S.-U.K. bombardment of Iraqi air defense positions shored up oil prices. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Brazilian real also slid, putting additional pressure on the peso, traders said. \par \par \uc2  However, the drop in the U.S. unemployment statistics published during the session helped reduce fears of a double-recession there, shoring up equity prices and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the peso, they added. \par \par \uc2  Despite the peso's fall, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has ruled out direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since it reflects current economic fundamentals, particularly in the oil and copper markets. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    - By Stephan Kueffner, Dow Jones Newswires; 562-460-8546;\par stephan.kueffner@dowjones.com\par    (Patricia San Juan contributed to this report.)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1170 1844 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020906dy9600139\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
