\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk Pres: Peso's Low No Reason For  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2002\par 19:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO -(Dow Jones)- Fluctuations in copper and oil prices are behind the current weakness of Chile's peso, and that will keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop it up, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Carlos Massad said Monday. \par \par \uc2  "What has been happening is reply of the dollar price  to international conditions. The price of copper has been  very low and the price of oil rising. We sell copper and buy oil, so both prices play against us," Massad said. \par \par \uc2  However, "the rise of the dollar tends to somewhat compensate (for) these negative effects, because it keeps stimulating exports despite the negative international price conditions," he added. \par \par \uc2  Once market conditions change, the peso will reverse course, he added. \par \par \uc2  The peso last week fell near its historic low of CLP718.70 to the dollar, but strengthened somewhat after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would issue dollar-denominated debt worth $220 million as part of an overall revamp of its debt-issuance practice. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't link the timing of the announcement to the peso's drop, but market participants have called the issuance of bonds in dollars one method the bank could use to quietly prop up the peso ahead of outright \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed Friday at CLP710.00 to the  dollar. \par \par \uc2  As long as there is no "exceptional situation," there would be no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Massad said. \par \par \uc2  However, "there are some who, taking advantage of the  country's situation, want to make an easy profit, but they've encountered surprises in the past, and I think they will again encounter surprises," he added. \par \par \uc2  -By Stephan Kueffner, Dow Jones Newswires; +562 460 8546; stephan.kueffner@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (Patricia San Juan contributed to this story) \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020902dy9200123\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
